# Round 18, C1-11 (fixed). Two replace rows of one input known the same day whose spans overlap (May 2026): neither
# is known before the other, so step 2 doesn't order them, step 3 doesn't either, and step 4 refuses the tie
# (LOAD-OVERLAP, L §4.6). snap11: LOAD-REPLACE two replace lines of rate known the same day.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input rate: money PLN
def r[d in days]: money PLN = rate at d
version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  rate = 100
version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-02-01
  replace rate = 150 governs 2026-03..2026-05
version v3
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-02-01
  replace rate = 170 governs 2026-05..2026-08
ask q: r[2026-01-15], r[2026-04-15], r[2026-06-15], r[2026-07-15]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-OVERLAP rows m.tally:19 and m.tally:24 of rate overlap at no keys, neither replacing the other (m.tally:24)
